issue.body:
With version 1.4.1 we had this issue: #8467
https://github.com/elasticsearch/elasticsearch/issues/8467

With 1.4.1 the workaround returns completely wrong results.
Example;

```
{
  "size" : 0,
  "query" : {
    "bool" : {
      "must" : [ {
        "range" : {
          "ts" : {
            "from" : "2015-02-13T00:00:00.0Z",
            "to" : "2015-02-13T23:59:58.0Z",
            "include_lower" : true,
            "include_upper" : true
          }
        }
      }, {
        "geo_shape" : {
          "loc" : {
            "shape" : {
              "type" : "polygon",
              "coordinates" : [ [ [ -179.999, 89.999 ], [ 179.999, 89.999 ], [ 179.999, -89.999 ], [ -179.999, -89.999 ], [ -179.999, 89.999 ] ] ]
            },
            "relation": "within"
          }
        }
      } ]
    }
  }
}
```

This returns 4360 results, which is clearly wrong.

Another query (only polygon changed a bit)

```
GET track_201502/_search
{
  "query": {
    "bool": {
      "must": [
        {
          "geo_shape": {
      "loc": {
        "shape": {
          "type": "polygon",
          "coordinates": [[[-180,90],[180,90],[180,-90],[-180,-90],[-180,90]]]
        },
        "relation": "within"
      }
    }
        },
        {
          "range": {
            "ts": {
              "from" : "2015-02-13T00:00:00.0Z",
            "to" : "2015-02-13T23:59:58.0Z",
            "include_lower" : true,
            "include_upper" : true
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ,
  "size": 0
}
```

This returns 6678451 results which is more likely .
As you can see the only difference between the 2 queries is the polygon .
Instead of 180/90 we have 179.999/89.999
This was workaround for  #8467
